From 5ba4f42ebe99608a683baa645ceae4da6aac8657 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skornuta <126527569+skornuta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:08:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/27] Memory minute: our buffers by call site; spare scratch
 trimmed (VICTORY_ALLOCATOR_TRIM=1)

- memtel: the host's buffer factories (upload, shared, GPU upload) take
  their caller's location (#[track_caller]) and count bytes and buffers
  alive by it, carried in the destruction callback's data (8 bits of
  site, 256 sites). The memory minute logs the 14 largest: what holds the
  ~1.1 GB of our CPU-visible buffers outside the host copies' CPU sides
  and the detile rings.
- With VICTORY_ALLOCATOR_TRIM=1, every ten seconds the spare scratch
  chunks that stayed kept the whole while (the fewest bytes kept since
  the last trim) are freed, oldest first. Chunks lists take and give back
  every frame stay; only the never-used surplus of the 128 MB cap goes
  (about 70 MB in the first area).

(cherry picked from commit 1626109e425195a17a5a89d98a926c0b1315b9b2)
